WHAT WAS TAKEN FROM UPSTREAM

  The algorithm, the numeric contract and the module structure. Every kernel in
  src/ops/ is a translation of src/core/k3_ops.c, and the same is true of src/st.rs,
  src/load.rs, src/trunk.rs, src/cache.rs, src/bind.rs, src/cfg.rs, src/tok/ and
  src/main.rs against their C counterparts. The floating-point evaluation order, the
  reduction trees, the tensor-name templates, the on-disk state format and the CLI
  surface are all upstream's design.

  fixtures/                     verbatim copy of upstream tests/fixtures/, including
                                the tiny-model oracle checkpoint and the per-kernel
                                reference outputs
  tools/tok_parity.py           verbatim
  tools/cmp_logits.py           verbatim
  tools/_paths.py               verbatim
  docs/images/_plots.py         the style helpers (style, bare, lollipop, save and the
                                colour palette) are derived from upstream
                                docs/images/_plots.py; the seven figures this file
                                renders are original to this port
  src/tok/                      a Rust transcription of upstream third_party/tok.h,
                                third_party/tok_unicode.h and
                                third_party/tok_unicode_o200k.h, which upstream had in
                                turn vendored from external projects (see the upstream
                                NOTICE below for their modification history), together
                                with src/tokenizer/k3_tok.h, which is upstream's own work

WHAT IS ORIGINAL TO THIS PORT

  The Rust implementation itself, including the explicit NEON and AVX2 kernels in
  src/ops/dispatch.rs and their lane derivations, the borrow-checked scratch carving,
  the WMat/Attn/ExpertSrc type surface, the test suite in tests/, benches/kernels.rs,
  the C-against-Rust measurements in docs/data/perf-sweep.csv and the figures in
  docs/images/.

NOT INCLUDED HERE

  Upstream's docs/ prose and its docs/data/ measurement captures, which were taken on
  upstream's hardware. Upstream's docs/kimi-k3-tech-report.pdf. Upstream's 115 figures
  explaining the model. Read all of these in the upstream repository.

